{"w":2400,"h":3396,"lines":[{"c":1,"x":0.82037266575568002,"h":0.016013072432842668,"y":0.035323820267319062,"t":"Reading","w":0.083454443613688256},{"x":0.061471566055370866,"w":0.79472035725911472,"y":0.074632969884607658,"t":"be less concerned with students' 'cognitive impatience', however, than by what may underlie","h":0.026997426935022939,"c":1},{"t":"it: the potential inability of large numbers of students to read with a level of critical analysis","w":0.78828089396158862,"x":0.061609491067068423,"c":1,"h":0.020439519758640112,"y":0.095975691152916154},{"y":0.11408453434610411,"c":1,"x":0.061634692687869877,"h":0.019960150701839652,"w":0.84176432291666659,"t":"sufficient to comprehend the complexity of thought and argument found in more demanding texts."},{"y":0.14885878817763154,"w":0.8151006062825521,"h":0.021252862415830465,"x":0.061559179537358094,"c":1,"t":"Multiple studies show that digital screen use may be causing a variety of troubling downstream"},{"h":0.022609146801125135,"c":1,"t":"effects on reading comprehension in older high school and college students. In Stavanger,","x":0.061555642804690745,"w":0.76788497924804688,"y":0.16500814839232469},{"t":"Norway, psychologist Anne Mangen and her colleagues studied how high school students","x":0.061591176768245173,"y":0.18453027454674042,"w":0.76568044026692705,"h":0.02055496939219903,"c":1},{"t":"comprehend the same material in different mediums. Mangen's group asked subjects questions","y":0.20045180108635308,"c":1,"h":0.023456018580424343,"x":0.061580335256374116,"w":0.80895553588867197},{"w":0.80478800455729171,"h":0.021484233465295821,"x":0.059544753630260058,"c":1,"t":"about a short story whose plot had universal student appeal; half of the students read the story","y":0.21986014404385745},{"y":0.23866773052025669,"c":1,"h":0.020462831423055161,"x":0.061610718436489645,"w":0.80269795735677074,"t":"on a tablet, the other half in paperback. Results indicated that students who read on print were"},{"x":0.059557533161417195,"w":0.82124226888020835,"c":1,"t":"superior in their comprehension to screen-reading peers, particularly in their ability to sequence","y":0.25537770913361824,"h":0.02141846475949416},{"w":0.4573744201660157,"y":0.27188972545035162,"c":1,"x":0.061439677397169275,"h":0.021302190630118623,"t":"detail and reconstruct the plot in chronological order."},{"w":0.82322769165039067,"x":0.059580486521573259,"h":0.019416791109370446,"c":1,"y":0.30919669262375349,"t":"Ziming Liu from San Jose State University has conducted a series of studies which indicate that"},{"y":0.32558139515936912,"c":1,"h":0.020413892990849059,"t":"theinew norm' in reading is skimming, involving word-spotting and browsing through the text.","w":0.81893005371093763,"x":0.05967077536915847},{"t":"Many readers now use a pattern when reading in which they sample the first line and then word-","y":0.34408531998761471,"w":0.82327992757161461,"x":0.059541923503470762,"h":0.021060790835898291,"c":1},{"y":0.36262775800794644,"t":"spot through the rest of the text. When the reading brain skims like this, it reduces time allocated","x":0.059555262847951554,"w":0.82738967895507809,"h":0.020596716513482161,"c":1},{"x":0.057494908973876303,"w":0.82944224039713532,"t":"to deep reading processes. In other words, we don't have time to grasp complexity, to understand","c":1,"y":0.38037386259960981,"h":0.021312026168769371},{"w":0.68930043538411456,"t":"another's feelings, to perceive beauty, and to create thoughts of the reader's own.","h":0.017667844522968212,"y":0.39958775025230298,"c":1,"x":0.059670769855169489},{"h":0.020552402671571324,"t":"The possibility that critical analysis, empathy and other deep reading processes could become","c":1,"x":0.059546798917941055,"y":0.4333168912021319,"w":0.80269973754882806},{"h":0.021320567675838786,"t":"the unintended 'collateral damage' of our digital culture is not a straightforward binary issue","w":0.79447453816731772,"y":0.45054388935391754,"c":1,"x":0.057504498480417963},{"t":"about print versus digital reading. It is about how we all have begun to read on various mediums","y":0.46870978277495656,"h":0.020752303591886512,"x":0.057515720939419923,"c":1,"w":0.82530665079752596},{"c":1,"y":0.48676060978249847,"x":0.057494534937715495,"w":0.81299372355143229,"h":0.020743923838764777,"t":"and how that changes not only what we read, but also the purposes for which we read. Nor is it"},{"t":"only about the young. The subtle atrophy of critical analysis and empathy affects us all equally. It","x":0.059577131013128809,"h":0.019988859780966539,"y":0.50498656188685198,"w":0.82939910888671864,"c":1},{"t":"affects our ability to navigate a constant bombardment of information. It incentivizes a retreat to","c":1,"y":0.52287906373222326,"x":0.057546993364073179,"w":0.82319285074869775,"h":0.01848849531337704},{"t":"the most familiar stores of unchecked information, which require and receive no analysis, leaving","y":0.54067546448413861,"x":0.057496428507477049,"w":0.83561208089192707,"h":0.02065276425634599,"c":1},{"t":"us susceptible to false information and irrational ideas.","x":0.057613160779361246,"h":0.017667844522968212,"c":1,"y":0.55800942311566548,"w":0.47325103759765624},{"x":0.057440697065387382,"y":0.5924678405672722,"t":"There's an old rule in neuroscience that does not alter with age: use it or lose it. It is a very","w":0.77608805338541675,"h":0.021260330056414034,"c":1},{"t":"hopeful principle when applied to critical thought in the reading brain because it implies choice.","y":0.6117182720079295,"w":0.8252428181966146,"h":0.019688142342898729,"c":1,"x":0.057539362672964958},{"y":0.62934336546731262,"t":"The story of the changing reading brain is hardly finished. We possess both the science and the","c":1,"w":0.8109326680501302,"h":0.020073427890018314,"x":0.057497928568394814},{"y":0.64625844754505712,"c":1,"h":0.021351545803398042,"x":0.055435950935760064,"w":0.83561879475911449,"t":"technology to identify and redress the changes in how we read before they become entrenched. If"},{"c":1,"t":"we work to understand exactly what we will lose, alongside the extraordinary new capacities that","x":0.057523833920347822,"w":0.83144922892252615,"h":0.01952407890832053,"y":0.66503390388352424},{"c":1,"y":0.68293658516237821,"t":"the digital world has brought us, there is as much reason for excitement as caution.","h":0.020835889944339381,"x":0.05748364815454475,"w":0.71012344360351565},{"x":0.86831275672592978,"c":1,"y":0.90843023238112497,"w":0.026748971939086874,"t":"87","h":0.013081395583944722},{"c":1,"y":0.95563027046131854,"x":0.71941411365393049,"t":"IELTSXpress.com","h":0.028416551605691898,"w":0.25443623860677067}]}